1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,424
Polymarket said 51% up. Bitcoin went down.
Noted.

2
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,503
Grudge grades prediction markets the way
weather forecasts are graded.

3
00:00:12,503 --> 00:00:17,307
Every five and fifteen minutes, it scores
each voice's call, and trusts the ones

4
00:00:17,307 --> 00:00:18,028
that verify.

5
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:21,568
Every wrong call goes into Grudge's memory
on Walrus.

6
00:00:21,568 --> 00:00:23,086
So let's wipe the server.

7
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:31,265
It reads Walrus and comes back. Same
trust.

8
00:00:31,265 --> 00:00:33,263
Same lesson. Nothing forgiven.

9
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:38,917
Lessons come back too. When DeepBook and
Polymarket disagree, DeepBook has been

10
00:00:38,917 --> 00:00:40,553
closer 84% of the time.

11
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:46,509
Four voices call the same Bitcoin move:
DeepBook on Sui, Polymarket, Kalshi, and

12
00:00:46,509 --> 00:00:47,173
the Crowd.

13
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:52,129
You can call it too. Pick up or down
before the lock, and the Crowd is graded

14
00:00:52,129 --> 00:00:53,197
like everyone else.

15
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:58,479
At the lock, the calls freeze. When the
window ends, every call is marked right or

16
00:00:58,479 --> 00:01:00,818
wrong against its voice, and trust moves.

17
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:07,381
Every grudge is a Walrus blob on mainnet.
Over a thousand memories so far:

18
00:01:07,381 --> 00:01:09,320
records, scoreboards, lessons.

19
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:19,421
This button rebuilds trust from Walrus
alone, and compares it with the live

20
00:01:19,421 --> 00:01:19,872
numbers.

21
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:25,773
Gap: zero.

22
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:32,366
Is it learning? Over the last 100
five-minute windows, Grudge scored 0.140,

23
00:01:32,366 --> 00:01:38,411
against 0.157 for a plain average.
DeepBook alone scores 0.139, so it hasn't

24
00:01:38,411 --> 00:01:40,480
beaten its best voice yet.

25
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:46,587
An agent asks for the line, gets a 402
with the price, pays in USDC, and asks

26
00:01:46,587 --> 00:01:48,197
again with the payment.

27
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,756
Here is a real one. About five cents of
USDC, settled on Sui.

28
00:01:53,756 --> 00:01:55,549
The agent needs no SUI.

29
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:06,661
DeepBook's odds, and every payment, are
read from Sui through Tatum.

30
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,962
Markets forget. Grudge doesn't.
